ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/174226229","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/5043#issuecomment-174226229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/5043","id":174226229,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3NDIyNjIyOQ==","user":{"login":"robertrossmann","id":3058150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTgxNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3058150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann","html_url":"https://github.com/robertrossmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-23T22:10:54Z","updated_at":"2016-01-23T22:10:54Z","body":"[I concur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/this).\n\nHowever, in the context of this rule, I still find it a little weird to be included here. Most of the time, we treat `this` as a variable holding the execution context, compared to \"things\" like `if`, `else`, `var`, `function`, `return` etc. which are used for control flow, declarations or other effects.\n\nI am genuinely curious to know what code would trigger this rule by improper spacing around `this` (except for my current issue with template strings). All the examples I could come up with are already covered in other rules and are mentioned in the examples detailing how this rule does not conflict with them. Thanks!\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/174226229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"robertrossmann","id":3058150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTgxNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3058150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann","html_url":"https://github.com/robertrossmann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertrossmann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":524056627,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDUyNDA1NjYyNw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/524056627","actor":{"login":"mysticatea","id":1937871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mzc4NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1937871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mysticatea","html_url":"https://githu